From: Etna Workload <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] relative_ref_drops_port_83adbc7 - Maybe-Scheme short-circuited port

Re-injection of the bug fixed by upstream commit
83adbc78cc64438a6d4fd4975e900f935baaee7c ("Fix bug: RelativeRef
serialization dropped port"). The buggy effectivePort did
"p <- authorityPort; scheme <- mScheme; dropPort scheme p", which
short-circuits to Nothing whenever there is no scheme - i.e. for every
RelativeRef. The fix splits dropPort into Nothing/Just-Scheme cases
and threads mScheme through directly so the Nothing case keeps the
port.

diff --git b/src/URI/ByteString/Internal.hs a/src/URI/ByteString/Internal.hs
index 07153e7..50a7e6b 100644
--- b/src/URI/ByteString/Internal.hs
+++ a/src/URI/ByteString/Internal.hs
@@ -320,10 +320,10 @@ serializeAuthority URINormalizationOptions {..} mScheme Authority {..} = BB.from
     port = maybe mempty packPort effectivePort
     effectivePort = do
       p <- authorityPort
-      scheme <- mScheme
-      dropPort scheme p
+      dropPort mScheme p
     packPort (Port p) = c8 ':' <> BB.fromString (show p)
-    dropPort scheme
+    dropPort Nothing = Just
+    dropPort (Just scheme)
       | unoDropDefPort = dropPort' scheme
       | otherwise = Just
     dropPort' s p
